### Project Limitations

This investigation used a synthetic dataset created for educational purposes. It was not connected to a live organisation or production environment.

The dataset was relatively small and contained limited authentication information. Therefore, the investigation demonstrates the process of analysing suspicious login behaviour rather than proving that a real cyberattack or account compromise occurred.

Further work could include investigating Windows authentication logs, correlating events from multiple sources, creating automated detection alerts and investigating additional indicators of compromise.

### Conclusion

This project gave me practical experience using Splunk Cloud as a SIEM platform and following a basic SOC investigation process.

I was able to identify suspicious authentication patterns, investigate the source IP and targeted accounts, analyse the timeline of events and present my findings in a monitoring dashboard and incident report.

Most importantly, I learned to interpret security logs, explain why activity may be suspicious and recognise the importance of gathering further evidence before reaching a conclusion.

These are skills I would like to continue developing as I work towards an entry-level cybersecurity role.
